Backport of nim-lang/Nim#24461 (upstream commit b7b1003e6a, devel 2024-11-21)
onto the 2.2.10 source tree.

For C compilers without __attribute__ (vcc), a {.packed.} object is wrapped
in `#pragma pack(push, 1)` / `#pragma pack(pop)`, and so is every branch
struct of a packed case object. The `addFieldWithStructType` template added
the branch's pop to `result`, the builder of the *calling* proc, instead of
`obj`, the union body it was building. In genRecordFieldsAux that `result`
is the enclosing record's field list, which is emitted before the union, so
the pops come out ahead of the pushes they are meant to close:

    #pragma pack(push, 1)
    struct PackedCase { tag; k;
    #pragma pack(pop)
    #pragma pack(pop)
    union { #pragma pack(push, 1) struct {...} _k_1;
            #pragma pack(push, 1) struct {...} _k_2; };
    };
    #pragma pack(pop)

Push and pop counts balance, but MSVC's pack stack is left one level deep,
so every struct emitted after a packed case object in that module is laid
out with pack(1) while other modules, and the compiler's own sizeof/offset
tables, use the natural layout. Found as sizeof(VariantArm) differing
between two translation units (65 vs 72 bytes) in nelli's MSVC CI. The
gcc/clang path uses __attribute__((__packed__)) per struct and is unaffected.

Regression from #24145 (the cbuilder introduction, which 2.2.x carries);
upstream fixed it in devel but never backported to version-2-2. The same
`result`/`obj` slip in `addStruct` is fixed here too: it is harmless today
only because every caller passes its own `result` as `obj`. Devel's
`finishStruct` writes to `obj`, so after this patch both templates match
devel. Drop this patch once a 2.2.x containing #24461 ships.

Repro: tests/packed_case_vcc.nim, checked by tests/check_packed_case_vcc.nim
(`--compileOnly --cc:vcc`, no MSVC needed).

--- a/compiler/cbuilder.nim
+++ b/compiler/cbuilder.nim
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
     obj.addField(name = "dummy", typ = "char")
   obj.add("};\n")
   if tfPacked in typ.flags and hasAttribute notin CC[m.config.cCompiler].props:
-    result.add("#pragma pack(pop)\n")
+    obj.add("#pragma pack(pop)\n")
 
 template addFieldWithStructType(obj: var Builder; m: BModule; parentTyp: PType; fieldName: string, body: typed) =
   ## adds a field with a `struct { ... }` type, building it according to `body`
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@
   obj.add(fieldName)
   obj.add(";\n")
   if tfPacked in parentTyp.flags and hasAttribute notin CC[m.config.cCompiler].props:
-    result.add("#pragma pack(pop)\n")
+    obj.add("#pragma pack(pop)\n")
 
 template addAnonUnion(obj: var Builder; body: typed) =
   obj.add "union{\n"
